 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.22,
   "text": "What would your country be like if the land masses were rotated by 90 degrees?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 3.76,
   "end": 6.88,
   "text": "Let's imagine that this alternate Earth develops over millions of years, giving time",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 6.88,
   "end": 9.08,
   "text": "for ecosystems and climate zones to settle out.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 9.54,
   "end": 10.98,
   "text": "Let's take a closer look at each continent.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 11.46,
   "end": 14.18,
   "text": "North America's climate is similar to before, but flipped north-south.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 14.72,
   "end": 18.26,
   "text": "Central America is now icy and polar, while Arctic Canada becomes tropical.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 19.22,
   "end": 21.56,
   "text": "Hurricanes threaten Greenland, Baffin Island, and the Maritimes.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 22.28,
   "end": 25.52,
   "text": "Tropical moisture from Baffin Bay in the former North Atlantic mixes with cool air",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 25.52,
   "end": 28.96,
   "text": "flowing down from the Rockies, creating a new tornado alley in the prairies inland",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 28.96,
   "end": 29.74,
   "text": "from Hudson Bay.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 30.24,
   "end": 31.92,
   "text": "South America looks sort of like the old Europe.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 32.26,
   "end": 35.36,
   "text": "It's cool and temperate along the Brazilian coast with grasslands and boreal",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 35.36,
   "end": 36.52,
   "text": "forests along much of its width.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 37.02,
   "end": 40.52,
   "text": "In the south, the boreal vegetation gives way to polar tundra and eventually to the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 40.52,
   "end": 44.02,
   "text": "massive icebound Andes, which cut the continent off from the frozen polar",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 44.02,
   "end": 47.84,
   "text": "waters. The Amazon, which in our world carries more water than the next seven",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 47.84,
   "end": 50.46,
   "text": "rivers put together, is reduced to something akin to the Mississippi.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 51.0,
   "end": 54.08,
   "text": "Asia is flipped in the same way North America was, with the Siberian coast",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 54.08,
   "end": 56.06,
   "text": "now facing an enclosed tropical sea.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.13,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 56.06,
   "end": 59.54,
   "text": "The Indian subcontinent and former Southeast Asia form the new Siberia.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 60.08,
   "end": 63.38,
   "text": "The Gobi Desert is no longer in the rain shadow of the Himalayas, but it doesn't",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 63.38,
   "end": 64.38,
   "text": "exactly become tropical.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 65.16,
   "end": 66.58,
   "text": "Europe resembles the old Southeast Asia.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 66.98,
   "end": 69.68,
   "text": "Great Britain and Ireland look like the islands of Sumatra and Borneo.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 69.96,
   "end": 73.42,
   "text": "Iceland resembles our Philippines, and Central Europe is the new New Guinea,",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 73.76,
   "end": 76.48,
   "text": "with the Alps the only place on the equator with permanent glaciers.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 77.24,
   "end": 81.12,
   "text": "Africa is rotated by 90 degrees, with former West Africa becoming tropical",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 81.12,
   "end": 83.74,
   "text": "rainforest and former East Africa an arid desert.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.139,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.022
  },
  {
   "start": 83.74,
   "end": 87.42,
   "text": "On our Earth, North America has by far the most tornadoes of any continent.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 87.84,
   "end": 90.5,
   "text": "But in this world, I bet they'd be frequent in Africa as well.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 91.3,
   "end": 94.46,
   "text": "Australia is cooler and wetter, with forests along the formerly dry western",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 94.46,
   "end": 96.9,
   "text": "regions. But Antarctica is the clear winner.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 97.26,
   "end": 99.5,
   "text": "Without its ice cap, it's a bit smaller than we remember.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 99.88,
   "end": 102.14,
   "text": "But most of it is blanketed with highland rainforest.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 102.52,
   "end": 104.84,
   "text": "There are alpine zones around the mountains to the south and west.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 105.24,
   "end": 108.76,
   "text": "The researchers at McMurdo and Ross Island work in a tropical paradise.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 109.32,
   "end": 112.26,
   "text": "If any of them decide they miss the frozen wastelands, hey, they can always",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 112.26,
   "end": 113.76,
   "text": "put in for a transfer to Costa Rica.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.269,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.026
  }
 ],
